Subject: [PATCH 1/2] media: ipu6: IPU4P: hold CPU latency at 100 us while the
 ISYS is powered

On the Surface Pro 7 (Ice Lake, C2 exit latency 253 us) the IR camera
stalls after a frame or two when the CPU may enter C2 during streaming
(ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE 300 us allows it): 0 of 10 starts delivered frames.
With 200 us or less every start streams (100/100 frames, 10/10 starts).
The request only applies while the ISYS is runtime-resumed.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
index 12498748c..b1517163d 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
@@ -103,6 +103,13 @@ enum ltr_did_type {
 };
 
 #define ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE	300
+/*
+ * IPU4P loses CSI-2 data when the CPU package sleeps deeper than C1 while
+ * streaming: on the Surface Pro 7 (C2 exit latency 253 us) the IR camera
+ * stalls after a frame or two at 300 us, and streams every time at 200 us
+ * or less.
+ */
+#define IPU4P_ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE	100
 
 static int
 ipu6_isys_csi2_fw_port_to_index(struct ipu6_isys *isys, unsigned int fw_port)
@@ -888,7 +895,9 @@ static int isys_runtime_pm_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	cpu_latency_qos_update_request(&isys->pm_qos, ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE);
+	cpu_latency_qos_update_request(&isys->pm_qos, IS_IPU4P(isp) ?
+				       IPU4P_ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE :
+				       ISYS_PM_QOS_VALUE);
 
 	ret = ipu6_buttress_start_tsc_sync(isp);
 	if (ret)
-- 
